---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HowToSchema from '../../components/seo/HowToSchema.astro';

const today = '2026-06-13T00:00:00+00:00';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is the Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator?',
    a: 'The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator is a free, privacy-first browser tool that calculates your engagement rate for Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, and LinkedIn. It shows the exact formula being used, lets you switch between followers, reach, or impressions as the denominator, and benchmarks your result against platform-specific averages. Everything runs instantly in your browser with no signup and no data collection.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I calculate my engagement rate on Instagram?',
    a: 'Add up your likes, comments, shares, and saves, then divide by your follower count and multiply by 100. For example, 500 total engagements on 10,000 followers equals a 5.0% engagement rate. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator also lets you switch the denominator to reach or impressions if you have access to those private metrics.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I calculate my engagement rate on TikTok?',
    a: 'Add your likes, comments, shares, and saves, then divide by total video views and multiply by 100. A video with 2,000 engagements and 50,000 views has a 4.0% engagement rate. Some brands also ask for a follower-based rate, so the Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator lets you toggle between views and followers.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is a good engagement rate on Instagram in 2026?',
    a: 'A good Instagram engagement rate typically falls between 1% and 3% for accounts with over 10,000 followers. Nano accounts under 10,000 followers often see 2% to 4%, while Reels and carousels usually outperform static posts by 30% to 50%. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator shows platform benchmarks tailored to your follower tier.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is a good engagement rate on TikTok in 2026?',
    a: 'A good TikTok engagement rate by views usually ranges from 5% to 8%. Nano creators with under 10,000 followers often hit 8% to 12%, while larger accounts typically see 3% to 6%. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator benchmarks your result against these ranges and explains whether your rate is below average, good, or excellent.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is engagement rate calculated by followers, reach, or impressions?',
    a: 'It depends on who is asking and which platform you use. The most common public formula divides total engagements by follower count. Reach-based and impressions-based formulas are more accurate but require private analytics access. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator lets you toggle all three denominators so you can match any brand or agency request.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why does my engagement rate drop when I gain followers?',
    a: 'This is completely normal. As your follower count grows, your content reaches a smaller percentage of your total audience unless your impressions scale proportionally. An account with 5,000 followers might see 4% engagement, while the same content at 50,000 followers drops to 1.5%. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator benchmarks your rate against others in your exact follower tier.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between Instagram Reels and static post engagement rates?',
    a: 'Reels typically generate higher engagement rates than static posts because the algorithm distributes them beyond your follower base through the Explore page. A static post might earn 1% to 2%, while a Reel from the same account can hit 2% to 4%. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator lets you select your content type so the benchmark comparison is accurate.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I calculate YouTube engagement rate for Shorts versus long-form videos?',
    a: 'For long-form videos, add likes, comments, and shares, then divide by subscriber count and multiply by 100. For Shorts, divide the same engagements by total views instead of subscribers because Shorts reach far more non-subscribers. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator switches the benchmarks automatically when you select your content type: just set the "Calculate by" denominator to Subscribers for long-form or Views for Shorts.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What counts as an engagement on LinkedIn?',
    a: 'On LinkedIn, engagements include reactions, comments, shares, and clicks. Reactions count as one engagement each, and document carousels often earn higher rates than text posts. Company pages typically see lower engagement than personal profiles. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator includes clicks in the LinkedIn formula and benchmarks separately for personal profiles and company pages.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What engagement rate do I need to get brand deals as a micro-influencer?',
    a: 'Most brands look for at least 2% to 4% engagement on Instagram or 5% to 8% on TikTok for micro-influencers with 10,000 to 50,000 followers. However, niche audience quality and content consistency often matter more than the raw percentage. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator helps you build a media kit with transparent formulas and benchmark context.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I calculate my engagement rate manually with real numbers?',
    a: 'Use the formula: total engagements divided by your chosen denominator, multiplied by 100. If your post gets 300 likes, 40 comments, 20 shares, and 10 saves, that is 370 total engagements. On 15,000 followers, your rate is 2.47%. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator performs this math instantly and shows the formula breakdown.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is considered a viral engagement rate on TikTok and Instagram?',
    a: 'On TikTok, a viral engagement rate by views is typically 10% or higher. On Instagram, viral feed posts often hit 5% to 8% by followers, though Reels can go higher because of algorithmic distribution. Remember that virality depends heavily on velocity: how fast engagements arrive in the first hour. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator shows where your rate sits on the benchmark scale.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I compare my Instagram engagement rate to my TikTok engagement rate?',
    a: 'No, direct comparison is misleading. TikTok engagement is usually calculated by views, while Instagram uses followers, and the platforms have different content distribution models. A 2% rate on Instagram and an 8% rate on TikTok can both represent strong performance for their respective platforms. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator normalizes benchmarks per platform so you compare against the right standard.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How often should I recalculate my engagement rate?',
    a: 'Calculate per post when testing content types, weekly when tracking campaigns, and monthly when updating your media kit or pitching brands. Avoid averaging one viral post with six months of normal posts, because a single outlier can distort your true performance. The Best Answer Hub Social Media Engagement Calculator lets you save and share specific calculations via URL for easy tracking.',
  },
];

const seo = {
  title: 'Social Media Engagement Calculator — Free (2026)',
  description: 'Calculate engagement rates for Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, and LinkedIn. Compare against platform benchmarks and export your report.',
  url: '/calculators/social-media-engagement/',
  type: 'WebPage' as const,
  datePublished: '2026-05-25T00:00:00+00:00',
  dateModified: today,
  breadcrumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Calculators', url: '/calculators/' },
    { name: 'Social Media Engagement Calculator', url: '/calculators/social-media-engagement/' }
  ],
  faq: faqs.map(f => ({ question: f.q, answer: f.a.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '').replace(/\s{2,}/g, ' ').trim() })),
};
---

<BaseLayout seo={seo}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="pt-10 pb-6 md:pt-14 md:pb-8">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-5">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-bae-primary-soft border border-bae-primary/15 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold text-bae-primary">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-bae-primary animate-pulse-dot"></span>
            Updated May 2026
          </div>
          <a href="/calculators/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink bg-white border border-bae-border px-3.5 py-2 rounded-bae-sm hover:border-bae-primary hover:text-bae-primary transition-colors no-underline shrink-0">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>
            Calculators
          </a>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-bae-ink mb-4">
          Social Media Engagement Calculator:<br/>
          <em class="italic text-bae-primary">See where you rank</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-base md:text-lg text-bae-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Calculate your engagement rate for Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, and LinkedIn. Switch between followers, reach, or impressions as the denominator and compare your result against platform benchmarks.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Calculator Interface -->
  <section class="py-6 md:py-8" aria-label="Social media engagement calculator">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 xl:grid-cols-[1fr_420px] gap-6 items-start">
        <!-- Left: Inputs -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <!-- Platform Tabs -->
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2" id="platform-tabs">
            <button type="button" data-platform="instagram" class="platform-tab active-tab px-4 py-2 rounded-bae-sm text-sm font-semibold border transition-colors">Instagram</button>
            <button type="button" data-platform="tiktok" class="platform-tab inactive-tab px-4 py-2 rounded-bae-sm text-sm font-semibold border transition-colors">TikTok</button>
            <button type="button" data-platform="youtube" class="platform-tab inactive-tab px-4 py-2 rounded-bae-sm text-sm font-semibold border transition-colors">YouTube</button>
            <button type="button" data-platform="linkedin" class="platform-tab inactive-tab px-4 py-2 rounded-bae-sm text-sm font-semibold border transition-colors">LinkedIn</button>
          </div>

          <!-- Inputs Card -->
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6 shadow-bae-sm">
            <h2 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-bae-muted mb-5">Engagement Metrics</h2>
            <div class="space-y-5">
              <!-- Audience -->
              <div>
                <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink block mb-2" id="label-audience">Followers</label>
                <input type="number" id="audience" min="0" value="10000" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
              </div>

              <!-- Denominator -->
              <div>
                <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink block mb-2">Calculate by</label>
                <select id="denominator" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary">
                  <option value="followers">Followers</option>
                  <option value="reach">Reach</option>
                  <option value="impressions">Impressions</option>
                </select>
              </div>

              <!-- Content Type -->
              <div id="content-type-wrapper">
                <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink block mb-2">Content Type</label>
                <select id="contentType" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary">
                  <option value="Reels">Reels</option>
                  <option value="Static Posts">Static Posts</option>
                  <option value="Carousels">Carousels</option>
                </select>
              </div>

              <!-- Follower Tier -->
              <div>
                <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink block mb-2">Account Size</label>
                <select id="followerTier" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary">
                  <option value="nano">Nano (1K – 10K)</option>
                  <option value="micro" selected>Micro (10K – 50K)</option>
                  <option value="mid">Mid (50K – 100K)</option>
                  <option value="macro">Macro (100K+)</option>
                </select>
              </div>

              <!-- Engagement Inputs -->
              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2 border-t border-bae-border">
                <div id="metric-wrap-0">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink block mb-2" id="label-metric-0">Likes</label>
                  <input type="number" id="metric-0" min="0" value="300" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
                </div>
                <div id="metric-wrap-1">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink block mb-2" id="label-metric-1">Comments</label>
                  <input type="number" id="metric-1" min="0" value="25" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
                </div>
                <div id="metric-wrap-2">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink block mb-2" id="label-metric-2">Shares</label>
                  <input type="number" id="metric-2" min="0" value="10" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
                </div>
                <div id="metric-wrap-3">
                  <label class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink block mb-2" id="label-metric-3">Saves</label>
                  <input type="number" id="metric-3" min="0" value="5" class="w-full text-sm border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm px-3 py-2 bg-white focus:outline-none focus:border-bae-primary" />
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex justify-end -mt-2 mb-1">
            <button type="button" id="reset-btn" class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-muted hover:text-bae-primary hover:underline transition-colors bg-transparent border-0 cursor-pointer px-0 py-0">
              Reset calculator
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Right: Results Panel -->
        <div class="xl:sticky xl:top-[84px] space-y-4">
          <!-- Main Result -->
          <div class="bg-bae-ink text-white rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6 shadow-bae-lg">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-white/60 mb-4">Engagement Rate</h3>
            <div class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold font-serif mb-1" id="result-rate">0.00%</div>
            <p class="text-xs text-white/50 mb-5" id="result-formula">Enter your metrics to calculate</p>

            <!-- Benchmark Bar -->
            <div class="space-y-3 border-t border-white/10 pt-4">
              <div class="relative h-3 bg-white/10 rounded-full overflow-hidden">
                <div id="bar-segment-avg" class="absolute left-0 top-0 h-full bg-white/30" style="width: 33%"></div>
                <div id="bar-segment-good" class="absolute top-0 h-full bg-bae-primary/60" style="left: 33%; width: 33%"></div>
                <div id="bar-segment-excellent" class="absolute top-0 h-full bg-bae-primary" style="left: 66%; width: 34%"></div>
                <div id="bar-user" class="absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-3 h-3 bg-white rounded-full border-2 border-bae-ink shadow" style="left: 0%"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-white/60">
                <span>Avg <span id="benchmark-avg">0%</span></span>
                <span>Good <span id="benchmark-good">0%</span></span>
                <span>Excellent <span id="benchmark-excellent">0%</span></span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-xs text-white/70 pt-1" id="benchmark-text">Enter your metrics to see your engagement rate.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Engagement Breakdown -->
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5 shadow-bae-sm">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-bae-muted mb-3">Engagement Breakdown</h3>
            <div class="space-y-2.5" id="breakdown-body">
              <!-- Populated by JS -->
            </div>
            <div class="border-t border-bae-border pt-2 mt-2">
              <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
                <span class="text-sm text-bae-muted">Total Engagements</span>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink" id="result-total-engagements">0</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <button type="button" id="pdf-btn" class="w-full bg-bae-ink hover:bg-bae-primary text-white font-semibold text-sm py-3 rounded-bae-sm transition-colors">
            Download PDF Report
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Report Summary (hidden on page; captured for PDF) -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border hidden" id="print-report">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-bae-ink mb-6">Engagement Rate Report</h2>
      <div class="bg-white border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-8 shadow-bae-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-[10px] flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold" style="background:#0f0f1a;color:#ffffff;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;">B<span style="color:#8b5cf6;">.</span></div>
          <div>
            <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink">Best Answer Hub</div>
            <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted">Social Media Engagement Report</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="border-t border-bae-border pt-4 mb-6">
          <!-- Top summary row -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-6">
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Engagement Rate</p>
              <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-bae-ink" id="report-rate">0.00%</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Total Engagements</p>
              <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary" id="report-total-engagements">0</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Platform</p>
              <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-ink" id="report-platform">Instagram</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- Settings row -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6 text-sm">
            <div>
              <span class="text-bae-muted">Content Type: </span>
              <span class="font-medium text-bae-ink" id="report-content-type">Reels</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="text-bae-muted">Calculated By: </span>
              <span class="font-medium text-bae-ink" id="report-denominator">Followers</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="text-bae-muted">Account Size: </span>
              <span class="font-medium text-bae-ink" id="report-tier">Micro (10K – 50K)</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="text-bae-muted">Audience Size: </span>
              <span class="font-medium text-bae-ink" id="report-audience">10,000</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- Benchmark row -->
          <div class="bg-bae-primary-soft border border-bae-primary/15 rounded-bae p-4 mb-6">
            <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Benchmark</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-bae-ink" id="report-benchmark">Average 0.00% / Good 0.00% / Excellent 0.00%</p>
          </div>
          <!-- Detailed metrics -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm" id="report-details">
            <!-- Populated by JS -->
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 text-xs text-bae-muted border-t border-bae-border pt-4">
          <p>Benchmarks are typical ranges reported by social media analysts as of May 2026. Actual performance varies by niche, content quality, posting frequency, and algorithm changes. Always verify engagement authenticity before making business decisions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <HowToSchema steps={[
    { name: 'Choose your platform', text: 'Select Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, or LinkedIn. The calculator automatically loads the right formula, engagement types, and benchmarks for that platform.' },
    { name: 'Enter your metrics', text: 'Input your audience size and engagement numbers. Toggle between followers, reach, impressions, views, or subscribers to match any brand or agency reporting standard.' },
    { name: 'See your benchmark', text: 'Get your engagement rate instantly with a visual benchmark bar showing where you rank (below average, good, or excellent) for your follower tier and content type.' },
  ]} />

  <!-- How It Works -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-bae-ink mb-8">How it works</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mb-3">1</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Choose your platform</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Select Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, or LinkedIn. The calculator automatically loads the right formula, engagement types, and benchmarks for that platform.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mb-3">2</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">Enter your metrics</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Input your audience size and engagement numbers. Toggle between followers, reach, impressions, views, or subscribers to match any brand or agency reporting standard.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-bae-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mb-3">3</div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">See your benchmark</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">Get your engagement rate instantly with a visual benchmark bar showing where you rank (below average, good, or excellent) for your follower tier and content type.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Related Tools CTA -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="bg-bae-primary-soft border border-bae-primary/15 rounded-bae p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">Explore more free calculators</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted">Also try our <a href="/calculators/roi-calculator/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">ROI Calculator</a>, <a href="/calculators/compound-interest/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Compound Interest Calculator</a>, and <a href="/calculators/" class="text-bae-primary hover:underline">Calculators Hub</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/calculators/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-bae-ink text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-bae-sm font-semibold text-sm no-underline hover:bg-bae-primary transition-colors shrink-0">
          Browse all calculators →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border" id="faq">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-bae-ink mb-8">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-6 max-w-4xl">
        {faqs.map((item) => (
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-bae-ink text-sm mb-2">{item.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">{item.a}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What People Calculate With It -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] font-bold text-bae-ink mb-8">What people calculate with it</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Influencer Pitch</div>
          <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">Micro-influencer media kit</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary font-serif mb-2">3.2% IG / 7.5% TikTok</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">A creator with 25,000 followers calculates Reels and static post rates separately to show brands exactly where their audience engages most.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Brand Due Diligence</div>
          <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">Campaign partner evaluation</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary font-serif mb-2">2.1% vs 4.8% benchmark</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">A marketing manager checks an influencer's engagement rate against platform averages before signing a $5,000 sponsorship contract.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Content Testing</div>
          <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">Reels versus carousel comparison</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary font-serif mb-2">Reels 4.2% / Carousels 2.8%</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">A social media manager runs side-by-side calculations to prove that video content drives 50% more engagement than static posts for their account.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Competitive Analysis</div>
          <div class="text-xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-1">Industry benchmark check</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-bae-primary font-serif mb-2">LinkedIn 1.5% / Industry 0.9%</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted leading-relaxed">A B2B SaaS founder measures their LinkedIn company page against the personal-profile average to justify increasing posting frequency.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-4">Scenarios are modeled estimates based on typical platform performance as of May 2026. Actual engagement varies by niche, content quality, and algorithm changes.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script slot="scripts" src="/html2pdf.bundle.min.js"></script>

  <script is:inline>
    (function() {
      const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);

      const config = {
        instagram: {
          name: 'Instagram',
          audienceLabel: 'Followers',
          denominators: [
            { value: 'followers', label: 'Followers' },
            { value: 'reach', label: 'Reach' },
            { value: 'impressions', label: 'Impressions' },
          ],
          metrics: [
            { key: 'likes', label: 'Likes' },
            { key: 'comments', label: 'Comments' },
            { key: 'shares', label: 'Shares' },
            { key: 'saves', label: 'Saves' },
          ],
          contentTypes: ['Reels', 'Static Posts', 'Carousels'],
          benchmarks: {
            'Reels': { nano: [2,4,6], micro: [1.5,3,5], mid: [1,2.5,4], macro: [0.8,2,3.5] },
            'Static Posts': { nano: [1.5,3,5], micro: [1,2.5,4], mid: [0.8,2,3.5], macro: [0.5,1.5,3] },
            'Carousels': { nano: [2,3.5,5.5], micro: [1.5,3,5], mid: [1,2.5,4.5], macro: [0.8,2,4] },
          }
        },
        tiktok: {
          name: 'TikTok',
          audienceLabel: 'Total Views',
          denominators: [
            { value: 'views', label: 'Views' },
            { value: 'followers', label: 'Followers' },
          ],
          metrics: [
            { key: 'likes', label: 'Likes' },
            { key: 'comments', label: 'Comments' },
            { key: 'shares', label: 'Shares' },
            { key: 'saves', label: 'Saves' },
          ],
          contentTypes: null,
          benchmarks: {
            'default': { nano: [5,8,12], micro: [4,7,10], mid: [3,6,9], macro: [2,5,8] },
          }
        },
        youtube: {
          name: 'YouTube',
          audienceLabel: 'Subscribers',
          denominators: [
            { value: 'subscribers', label: 'Subscribers' },
            { value: 'views', label: 'Views' },
          ],
          metrics: [
            { key: 'likes', label: 'Likes' },
            { key: 'comments', label: 'Comments' },
            { key: 'shares', label: 'Shares' },
          ],
          contentTypes: ['Shorts', 'Long-form'],
          benchmarks: {
            'Shorts': { nano: [3,5,8], micro: [3,5,8], mid: [3,5,8], macro: [3,5,8] },
            'Long-form': { nano: [2,4,6], micro: [2,4,6], mid: [2,4,6], macro: [2,4,6] },
          }
        },
        linkedin: {
          name: 'LinkedIn',
          audienceLabel: 'Followers',
          denominators: [
            { value: 'followers', label: 'Followers' },
            { value: 'impressions', label: 'Impressions' },
          ],
          metrics: [
            { key: 'reactions', label: 'Reactions' },
            { key: 'comments', label: 'Comments' },
            { key: 'shares', label: 'Shares' },
            { key: 'clicks', label: 'Clicks' },
          ],
          contentTypes: ['Personal Profile', 'Company Page'],
          benchmarks: {
            'Personal Profile': { nano: [1,3,6], micro: [1,3,6], mid: [1,3,6], macro: [1,3,6] },
            'Company Page': { nano: [0.3,1,3], micro: [0.3,1,3], mid: [0.3,1,3], macro: [0.3,1,3] },
          }
        }
      };

      const defaults = {
        platform: 'instagram',
        audience: 10000,
        followerTier: 'micro',
        metrics: [300, 25, 10, 5]
      };

      let currentPlatform = defaults.platform;

      function getDefaultDenominator(platform) {
        return config[platform].denominators[0].value;
      }

      function getDefaultContentType(platform) {
        const c = config[platform].contentTypes;
        return c ? c[0] : 'default';
      }

      function formatNumber(n) {
        return n.toLocaleString(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: 0 });
      }

      function formatPercent(n) {
        return n.toFixed(2) + '%';
      }

      function updatePlatformUI() {
        const p = config[currentPlatform];

        document.querySelectorAll('.platform-tab').forEach(btn => {
          if (btn.dataset.platform === currentPlatform) {
            btn.classList.add('active-tab');
            btn.classList.remove('inactive-tab');
          } else {
            btn.classList.remove('active-tab');
            btn.classList.add('inactive-tab');
          }
        });

        const denomSelect = $('denominator');
        denomSelect.innerHTML = '';
        p.denominators.forEach(d => {
          const opt = document.createElement('option');
          opt.value = d.value;
          opt.textContent = d.label;
          denomSelect.appendChild(opt);
        });

        const ctWrap = $('content-type-wrapper');
        const ctSelect = $('contentType');
        if (p.contentTypes) {
          ctWrap.style.display = 'block';
          ctSelect.innerHTML = '';
          p.contentTypes.forEach(ct => {
            const opt = document.createElement('option');
            opt.value = ct;
            opt.textContent = ct;
            ctSelect.appendChild(opt);
          });
        } else {
          ctWrap.style.display = 'none';
        }

        for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
          const wrap = $('metric-wrap-' + i);
          const label = $('label-metric-' + i);
          if (i < p.metrics.length) {
            label.textContent = p.metrics[i].label;
            wrap.style.display = 'block';
          } else {
            wrap.style.display = 'none';
            $('metric-' + i).value = 0;
          }
        }

        updateAudienceLabel();
      }

      function updateAudienceLabel() {
        const p = config[currentPlatform];
        const selected = $('denominator').value;
        const found = p.denominators.find(d => d.value === selected);
        $('label-audience').textContent = found ? found.label : p.audienceLabel;
      }

      function calculate() {
        const p = config[currentPlatform];
        const denomValue = parseFloat($('audience').value) || 0;
        const followerTier = $('followerTier').value;
        const contentType = p.contentTypes ? $('contentType').value : 'default';
        const contentTypeDisplay = p.contentTypes ? contentType : 'All content';
        const ctPhrase = p.contentTypes ? (' ' + contentType) : '';

        let totalEngagements = 0;
        const breakdown = [];
        for (let i = 0; i < p.metrics.length; i++) {
          const val = parseFloat($('metric-' + i).value) || 0;
          totalEngagements += val;
          breakdown.push({ label: p.metrics[i].label, value: val });
        }

        const rate = denomValue > 0 ? (totalEngagements / denomValue) * 100 : 0;

        $('result-rate').textContent = formatPercent(rate);
        $('result-total-engagements').textContent = formatNumber(totalEngagements);

        const denomLabel = $('denominator').options[$('denominator').selectedIndex].text;
        $('result-formula').textContent =
          p.name + ': (' + breakdown.map(b => b.label).join(' + ') + ') / ' + denomLabel + ' \u00d7 100';

        const bench = (p.benchmarks[contentType] || p.benchmarks['default'] || {})[followerTier] || [0,0,0];
        const [avg, good, excellent] = bench;

        $('benchmark-avg').textContent = formatPercent(avg);
        $('benchmark-good').textContent = formatPercent(good);
        $('benchmark-excellent').textContent = formatPercent(excellent);

        const maxBar = Math.max(excellent * 1.5, rate, 0.1);
        const barAvg = Math.min(100, (avg / maxBar) * 100);
        const barGood = Math.min(100, ((good - avg) / maxBar) * 100);
        const barExc = Math.min(100, ((excellent - good) / maxBar) * 100);
        const barUser = Math.min(100, (rate / maxBar) * 100);

        $('bar-segment-avg').style.width = barAvg + '%';
        $('bar-segment-good').style.left = barAvg + '%';
        $('bar-segment-good').style.width = barGood + '%';
        $('bar-segment-excellent').style.left = (barAvg + barGood) + '%';
        $('bar-segment-excellent').style.width = barExc + '%';
        $('bar-user').style.left = barUser + '%';

        let interp = '';
        if (rate >= excellent) interp = 'Excellent \u2014 your engagement rate is in the top tier for ' + p.name + ctPhrase + '.';
        else if (rate >= good) interp = 'Good \u2014 your engagement rate is above average for ' + p.name + ctPhrase + '.';
        else if (rate >= avg) interp = 'Average \u2014 your engagement rate is typical for ' + p.name + ctPhrase + '.';
        else if (rate > 0) interp = 'Below average \u2014 there is room to improve your ' + p.name + ctPhrase + ' engagement.';
        else interp = 'Enter your metrics to see your engagement rate.';
        $('benchmark-text').textContent = interp;

        const bdContainer = $('breakdown-body');
        bdContainer.innerHTML = '';
        breakdown.forEach(b => {
          const pct = totalEngagements > 0 ? ((b.value / totalEngagements) * 100).toFixed(1) : 0;
          const row = document.createElement('div');
          row.className = 'flex justify-between items-center';
          const s1 = document.createElement('span');
          s1.className = 'text-sm text-bae-muted';
          s1.textContent = b.label;
          const s2 = document.createElement('span');
          s2.className = 'text-sm font-semibold text-bae-ink';
          s2.textContent = formatNumber(b.value) + ' (' + pct + '%)';
          row.appendChild(s1);
          row.appendChild(s2);
          bdContainer.appendChild(row);
        });

        const tierText = $('followerTier').options[$('followerTier').selectedIndex].text;

        const reportFields = [
          ['report-rate', formatPercent(rate)],
          ['report-platform', p.name],
          ['report-content-type', contentTypeDisplay],
          ['report-denominator', denomLabel],
          ['report-tier', tierText],
          ['report-audience', formatNumber(denomValue)],
          ['report-total-engagements', formatNumber(totalEngagements)],
          ['report-benchmark', 'Average ' + formatPercent(avg) + ' / Good ' + formatPercent(good) + ' / Excellent ' + formatPercent(excellent)],
        ];
        reportFields.forEach(([id, val]) => {
          const el = $(id);
          if (el) el.textContent = val;
        });

        const reportDetails = $('report-details');
        if (reportDetails) {
          reportDetails.innerHTML = '';
          const detailRows = [
            ['Platform', p.name],
            ['Content Type', contentTypeDisplay],
            ['Denominator', denomLabel],
            ['Account Size', tierText],
            ['Audience Size', formatNumber(denomValue)],
          ];
          breakdown.forEach(b => {
            detailRows.push([b.label, formatNumber(b.value)]);
          });
          detailRows.push(['Total Engagements', formatNumber(totalEngagements)]);
          detailRows.push(['Engagement Rate', formatPercent(rate)]);
          detailRows.forEach(([label, value]) => {
            const div = document.createElement('div');
            const s1 = document.createElement('span');
            s1.className = 'text-bae-muted';
            s1.textContent = label + ': ';
            const s2 = document.createElement('span');
            s2.className = 'font-medium text-bae-ink';
            s2.textContent = value;
            div.appendChild(s1);
            div.appendChild(s2);
            reportDetails.appendChild(div);
          });
        }

        updateURL();
      }

      function updateURL() {
        try {
          const url = new URL(window.location.href);
          const params = new URLSearchParams();

          if (currentPlatform !== defaults.platform) params.set('platform', currentPlatform);

          const p = config[currentPlatform];
          const audience = parseFloat($('audience').value) || defaults.audience;
          const contentType = p.contentTypes ? $('contentType').value : null;
          const followerTier = $('followerTier').value;
          const denom = $('denominator').value;

          if (audience !== defaults.audience) params.set('audience', audience);
          if (denom !== getDefaultDenominator(currentPlatform)) params.set('denom', denom);
          if (followerTier !== defaults.followerTier) params.set('tier', followerTier);
          if (contentType && contentType !== getDefaultContentType(currentPlatform)) params.set('type', contentType);

          for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            const val = parseFloat($('metric-' + i).value) || defaults.metrics[i];
            if (val !== defaults.metrics[i]) params.set('m' + i, val);
          }

          url.search = params.toString();
          window.history.replaceState({}, '', url);
        } catch (e) {}
      }

      function readURL() {
        try {
          const url = new URL(window.location.href);
          const platform = url.searchParams.get('platform');
          if (platform && config[platform]) {
            currentPlatform = platform;
          }
          updatePlatformUI();

          const audience = url.searchParams.get('audience');
          if (audience !== null) $('audience').value = audience;

          const denom = url.searchParams.get('denom');
          if (denom !== null && Array.from($('denominator').options).some(o => o.value === denom)) {
            $('denominator').value = denom;
            updateAudienceLabel();
          }

          const tier = url.searchParams.get('tier');
          if (tier !== null) $('followerTier').value = tier;

          const type = url.searchParams.get('type');
          if (type !== null && Array.from($('contentType').options).some(o => o.value === type)) {
            $('contentType').value = type;
          }

          for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            const val = url.searchParams.get('m' + i);
            if (val !== null) $('metric-' + i).value = val;
          }
        } catch (e) {}
      }

      document.querySelectorAll('.platform-tab').forEach(btn => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          currentPlatform = btn.dataset.platform;
          updatePlatformUI();
          calculate();
        });
      });

      $('audience').addEventListener('input', calculate);
      $('denominator').addEventListener('change', () => {
        updateAudienceLabel();
        calculate();
      });
      $('followerTier').addEventListener('change', calculate);
      $('contentType').addEventListener('change', calculate);
      for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
        $('metric-' + i).addEventListener('input', calculate);
      }

      $('reset-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
        currentPlatform = defaults.platform;
        updatePlatformUI();
        $('audience').value = 0;
        $('followerTier').value = defaults.followerTier;
        $('denominator').value = getDefaultDenominator(currentPlatform);
        updateAudienceLabel();
        if (config[currentPlatform].contentTypes) {
          $('contentType').value = getDefaultContentType(currentPlatform);
        }
        for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
          $('metric-' + i).value = 0;
        }
        window.history.replaceState({}, '', window.location.pathname);
        calculate();
      });

      $('pdf-btn').addEventListener('click', async () => {
        if (typeof html2pdf === 'undefined') return;
        const btn = $('pdf-btn');
        const originalText = btn.textContent;
        btn.textContent = 'Generating PDF...';
        btn.disabled = true;

        const wrapper = document.createElement('div');
        wrapper.style.width = '210mm';
        wrapper.style.boxSizing = 'border-box';
        wrapper.style.margin = '0';

        const report = $('print-report').cloneNode(true);
        report.removeAttribute('id');
        report.classList.remove('hidden');
        wrapper.appendChild(report);
        document.body.appendChild(wrapper);

        try {
          await html2pdf().set({
            margin: [8, 8, 8, 8],
            filename: 'social-media-engagement-report.pdf',
            image: { type: 'jpeg', quality: 0.95 },
            pagebreak: { mode: ['css', 'legacy'], avoid: 'p, li, div, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, ul, tr, td, table' },
            html2canvas: { scale: 2, useCORS: true, logging: false, scrollX: 0, scrollY: 0 },
            jsPDF: { unit: 'mm', format: 'a4', orientation: 'portrait' }
          }).from(wrapper).save();
        } catch (err) {
          console.error(err);
        } finally {
          if (wrapper.parentNode) document.body.removeChild(wrapper);
          btn.textContent = originalText;
          btn.disabled = false;
        }
      });

      readURL();
      calculate();
    })();
  </script>

  <style>
    @media print {
      body * { visibility: hidden; }
      #print-report, #print-report * { visibility: visible; }
      #print-report { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 100%; display: block !important; }
      #print-report .container { max-width: 100% !important; padding: 0 !important; }
      nav, footer, section:not(#print-report), main > *:not(#print-report) { display: none !important; }
    }
    .active-tab {
      background-color: #6366f1;
      color: white;
      border-color: #6366f1;
    }
    .inactive-tab {
      background-color: white;
      color: #374151;
      border-color: #e5e7eb;
    }
    .inactive-tab:hover {
      border-color: #6366f1;
      color: #6366f1;
    }
  </style>

